WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.101
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.102
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.136
I hope everyone's
doin' well tonight

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.604
and let's get to the news.

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.808
Well, just this week,
we learned that women received

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:12.345
unnecessary hysterectomies
at a ICE detention facility,

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.481
the attorney general called
for demonstrators

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:16.015
to be charged with sedition,

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.250
and the White House wanted
to use a heat ray

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.387
on peaceful protesters to clear
the way for a photo op.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:25.191
I think, at this point,
even Q is an undecided voter.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:28.060
That's right, federals officials
reportedly considered deploying

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.262
a so-called heat ray

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:33.032
that makes targets' skin
feel like it's burning,

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.901
in preparation for clearing
a peaceful protest

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.436
across from the White House
in June.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.171
Apparently, they decided
the ray was too much,

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:42.208
after testing it
on Steve Bannon.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.776
[ Laughing ]
Looks like the heat ray

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:44.911
was accidently set to...

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.347
Multiple White House staffers

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:51.250
reportedly tested positive
yesterday for the coronavirus,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.686
except for Stephen Miller,
who, thankfully,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.121
wears a mask.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.022
That's right,
multiple White House staffers

00:00:57.022 --> 00:00:59.859
reportedly tested positive
yesterday for the coronavirus.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:00.860
But don't worry.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.028
They're downplaying it,

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.862
so he doesn't panic.

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:06.232
Former President Barack Obama
announced today

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:11.237
that the 768-page
first volume of his memoir

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.205
will be titled
the "Promised Land."

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:16.776
Seems really long, but remember,
most of that is pauses.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.677
[ As Obama ]
Chapter, uh...

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:20.279
one!

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.315
[ Laughing ]
President Trump spoke today

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.751
at the White House Conference
on American History.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.454
This year's theme was
"Doomed to Repeat Itself."

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.057
Barbados announced this week
that it will remove

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.592
Britain's Queen Elizabeth
as its head of state

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.661
and become a republic
by next year

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:38.030
and the British press
has already figured out

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.166
who to blame.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.301
According to a new report,

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:44.036
leafy green produce
has been linked

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:49.208
to 40 serious E. coli outbreaks
from 2009 to 2018.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:52.912
Wow, that stuff could
really kale you.
["kill"]

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:57.150
I guess eating leafy greens
escarole of the dice.
["is a roll"]

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.051
But, look, if you ate some,

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:01.120
just romaine calm
["remain"]

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.287
and lettuce hope it
["let us"]

00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:04.190
doesn't happen again.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.292
Also, sorry
if this joke gave you

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.962
an arugula heartbeat.
["irregular"]

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.531
You know, when I get the jokes,

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.366
I get the name
of who wrote them.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.768
That one was written
by two writers.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:20.005
Ian and Bryan had
to collaborate on that.

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:22.942
I'm assuming at a Whole Foods.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.777
Keep up the great work, guys.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.112
I really miss seeing your faces.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.115
[ Laughing ]
Finally --

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:31.384
And, finally,
the owners of Chuck E. Cheese

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.087
have petitioned
a Texas bankruptcy court

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.889
to allow them to destroy more
than seven billion prize tickets

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.058
that have piled up
in its supply chain

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.526
amid the coronavirus pandemic.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:44.030
Seven billion tickets or,
if you convert that to prizes,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.731
[ Laughing ]
one large bear.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:48.601
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

